      {
        "index": 41,
        "name": "Throw Me a Bone!",
        "description": "MENU: “There has to be a logical reason for this world to be like this.”\nMENU: “Even if we’ve gotta tear out all our existing notions of reality and start from scratch, there still have to be answers and we can find them.”\nMENU: “A scientist wouldn't just give up on understanding the world because it threw them a curveball like pipes fossilized in Jurassic bedrock.”\nMENU: “There are always answers and the scientific method can lead us to them.”\nMENU: “Keep scavenging around inside the caves with your Kami, we need more data.”\nMENU: “We’ve got to observe the environment so that we can orient ourselves to it.\nMENU: “So get out there and do some observing!”",
